WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:04.800
Landing a role in a superhero movie comes
with more than just a nice paycheck and a

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:05.920
steady work opportunity.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:10.540
Actors are now expected to get in superhuman
shape for action roles, and Margot Robbie

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:12.600
as Harley Quinn is no exception.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.180
Here's how she got into havoc-wreaking shape.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:21.160
Of course Margot Robbie is fully dedicated
to playing Harley Quinn now, but she originally

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:24.200
got the role without even having to convince
anyone she wanted it.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:29.300
The actress told MTV News that the team behind
Suicide Squad approached her with the role,

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.900
offering her the part without even having
to audition.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:37.140
"I actually got offered this one, I didn't
audition, which is a real step up as an actor

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:38.780
when you can get offered things."

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:43.440
As it turns out, the producers were captivated
by Robbie's performance alongside Will Smith

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.530
in the 2015 movie Focus.

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:50.260
Smith was already locked in to play Deadshot,
and Suicide Squad wanted to recreate that

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:52.420
connection when they cast their Harley Quinn.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.860
"I guess they knew that Will and I worked
well together, so that was a given.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:58.680
We didn't have to do chemistry reads or anything
like that."

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.180
The studio's gamble paid off, and while the
overall reviews for Suicide Squad were less

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:07.859
than enthusiastic, the dynamic between Smith
and Robbie was a consistent high point of

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:08.360
the film.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.079
"You're my friend too."

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:13.940
"Stay evil, dollface."

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:19.500
Margot Robbie is already in pretty great shape,
thanks to working out four or five times a

00:01:19.509 --> 00:01:24.049
week for an hour each session, according to
Hollywood personal trainer Andie Hecker.

00:01:24.049 --> 00:01:28.689
To get in fighting shape for her comic book
movie, however, she ramped that up to three

00:01:28.689 --> 00:01:29.700
hours per day.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:34.430
As part of a ballet-based fitness program
that Hecker operates, Robbie worked out in

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:38.560
three-hour blocks nearly every day for three
weeks while filming Suicide Squad.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:43.159
Hecker told People magazine that the focus
on Harley's body and her skimpy costume pushed

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:45.080
Robbie to work out that much harder.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:46.140
According to Hecker,

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:50.880
"There's a scene in Suicide Squad where she
changes clothes in front of a bunch of dudes,

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:53.100
so her abs needed to be impeccable.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:57.720
And in those tiny shorts Harley wears, her
butt was constantly on display."

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:02.560
The parts of Robbie's body that were onscreen
for most of Suicide Squad became the focus

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:03.800
of her tailored workouts.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:08.580
Hecker came up with an exercise routine that
would transform Robbie from a glamorous starlet

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:10.820
into the tough and acrobatic Harley Quinn.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.000
According to Hecker,

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:14.340
"[Margot] wanted to lean out and tone up.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:18.060
She’s already slender, but we wanted to
make her a little stronger.”

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:22.970
To achieve these goals, most of Robbie's workout
regimen consisted of non-bulking cardio exercises

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:24.060
like ballet jumps.

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:28.700
As a former dancer who runs a ballet training
program, Hecker told People that the jumps

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:33.940
ballet dancers perform are, quote, "surprisingly
the most challenging form of cardio I have

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:35.140
ever come across."

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:40.110
But despite the relative difficulty of the
exercises, Hecker said that Robbie rarely

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:42.320
ever faltered in her commitment to the routine.

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:46.900
Hecker compared Robbie to a machine when she
spoke to the Los Angeles Times.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:51.510
The actress' workouts apparently resembled
dance marathons, where other clients of Hecker's

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:55.380
would steadily throw in the towel while Robbie
kept at it, relentlessly.

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:56.640
Hecker shared that,

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:59.220
"Other people would try [the workout] along
with us.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:02.140
But she kept going when other people were
dropping off.

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:07.340
It's so challenging to keep up that level
of intensity, but she powered through it."

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:12.340
Hecker also ran the actress through a weightlifting
regimen intended to tone her butt, thighs

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:13.040
and legs.

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:18.280
She spoke of Robbie's workout on a granular
level in the lead-up to Suicide Squad's release,

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:23.020
telling publications the exact types of exercises
Robbie went through while trying to embody

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:23.720
Harley Quinn.

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:29.090
She said that they went for a lower number
of reps with more weight, a focus on form,

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:31.630
and engaging the correct muscle groups.

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:34.680
In an interview with The Hollywood Reporter,
Hecker explained,

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:37.000
"She had to look sexy and strong.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:42.340
We'd do lower reps, so 20 leg lifts with that
ankle weight on and then take a break to move

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:46.720
on to the other leg to do another 20, making
sure her glutes were doing it and not her

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:47.720
hamstrings."

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:52.880
If that robotic intensity is making you feel
like you'll never be able to attain a form

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.840
like Margot Robbie's, don't worry.

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:59.460
While Hecker painted a picture of the actress
as an ultra-dedicated workhorse in the gym,

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:03.440
Robbie herself revealed that she is far from
disciplined when it comes to her diet.

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:08.100
In an interview with Emirates Woman, Robbie
admitted that she can't handle calorie-cutting

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:12.140
diets, and that cutting delicious and fatty
foods from her life makes her "miserable."

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:14.100
"I'm not good at doing moderation.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:17.780
I can't just have a salad every day and a
half a glass of wine every second day.

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:18.480
I can't do it."

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:23.860
Robbie told the publication that her diet
largely consisted of beer, fries and burgers,

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:25.200
which she burned off in the gym.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:29.370
She added that she has a rather unhealthy
way of cutting weight quickly, if a role calls

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:30.370
for it, saying,

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:34.420
"If I have to get in a bikini then I'll eat
carrot sticks for three days.

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:36.250
I'm one extreme or the other."

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:41.820
Successfully pushing to get a standalone Harley
Quinn movie made meant that Robbie had to

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:46.580
get back into Suicide Squad shape, in which
she was able to perform most of her own stunts.

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:49.580
According to Suicide Squad co-producer Andy
Horwitz,

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:53.400
"Margot does 97% of her own stunts in this
movie.

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:57.380
She embraced everything we threw at her, she
makes it her own and does it better than we

00:04:57.380 --> 00:04:59.040
could've ever assumed it was going to be."

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:03.380
However, when it came to revisiting Harley
for Birds of Prey, Robbie said many of the

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:06.780
stunts in the new film were actually too dangerous
to take on.

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:11.320
"There's a lot of really cool stunts in the
Birds Of Prey movie.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:14.930
Quite a few of them, I couldn't do, because
they were just too risky."

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:19.100
That's not to say that Robbie slacked off
in comparison to her work for Suicide Squad,

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:19.600
though.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:24.760
In addition to regular workouts, Robbie trained
to roller skate ahead of Birds of Prey, after

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:27.910
already learning to ice skate for her role
in I, Tonya.

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:32.500
Photos of Robbie training and shooting in
roller skates circulated on comic book blogs

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:37.030
ahead of the movie's release, revealing that
Prey will be based on a later version of Harley

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:39.200
Quinn modeled after roller derby players.

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:45.230
The roller-skating Harley Quinn comes from
the New 52 reboot in the DC Universe, which

00:05:45.230 --> 00:05:48.960
remodeled many characters with a hard refresh
of 52 titles.

00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:52.700
Even a newish character like Quinn was not
immune from the mandate.

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:56.860
The most recent version of Quinn has been
completely removed from the Joker, as she

00:05:56.860 --> 00:06:00.020
finally split with the Clown Prince of Crime
for good.

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:04.000
With her newfound independence, Quinn's motivations
have also shifted.

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:09.160
Where before most of her actions could be
explained as working for "Mr. J," the newly

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:11.780
single Quinn is considerably less villainous.

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:17.830
She's become a sort-of antiheroic vigilante,
toeing the line between criminal and superhero

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:20.780
while attempting to hold her home of Coney
Island together.

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:26.210
The new Quinn is in the mold of wisecracking
weirdos with murky morals like Deadpool, and

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:30.280
screenwriter Christina Hodson even cited the
"Merc with a Mouth" when she talked about

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:32.720
her early talks with Margot Robbie around
the film.

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:37.160
Robbie's dedication to the character is bound
to translate to the big screen once again,

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:38.880
as it did in Suicide Squad.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:43.300
And considering that Birds of Prey's reviews
are a big improvement over the reaction to

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:47.800
Suicide Squad, it's likely that we will be
seeing Robbie as a ripped Harley Quinn for

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:48.680
years to come.

